{"id": "EUVD-2026-82033", "enisaUuid": "c3cfa727-e183-3e6f-9454-edae42e5e848", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: avoid nss underflow in mt7915_mcu_get_sta_nss\n\nIf a peer's VHT/HE MCS map has no supported spatial stream (all fields\n0x3), the loop exits with nss == 0 and the function returned (u8)-1 (255),\nwhich was then written into the firmware sta_rec_bf beamforming fields.\nClamp the result to 0.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2801477c36a19be4f549fe60e54995f03b0ea7b9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38f4d6323bcd65e41a691432eddabd2b03acdeee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25f753f7f620955a8a51e63e445d8b9076c51396", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e63c6291ecddf94769ab91f9d8cdb6ca939f7fc6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85bd46ab7674b6d357f9a14791352c65fb09eee9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ce78d04c7ea4b66838941b5a4232dd1ee0e2cc7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecfd1a07e78c31d81322fb2d81dc468081cc3004", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a2f4be532e3ea4e2b536e411793a05aaa51af25"], "aliases": ["GHSA-934p-6j28-7ggx", "CVE-2026-90372"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b5229e9-2ebd-3026-b429-a8147a272d42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89029a85482cbcf68026a89fc974e8f6898d6b37 <38f4d6323bcd65e41a691432eddabd2b03acdeee"}, {"id": "1000c7c6-f70d-3128-a1fd-e2983a98cad5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89029a85482cbcf68026a89fc974e8f6898d6b37 <4a2f4be532e3ea4e2b536e411793a05aaa51af25"}, {"id": "26166eba-5389-37b0-ab14-8940b0f42d9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "3e8e6a20-c226-3b28-ad9a-1e40c858